#text(8.8pt)[
- #rich((("t", "Tool and scenario: perf/k6/README.​md §V2 and perf/k6/browse.​js: grafana/k6:1.6.1 pinned by digest; ramping-arrival executor, 10, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100, 125, 150, 175, 200 iterations/s, 60 s each; one request per iteration, 7 list : 3 detail; no sleep; 100 preallocated VUs, 400 max; 10 s request timeout; gates per plateau p95 < 500 ms, error rate < 1%, zero dropped iterations (calibrate.​mjs). Anonymous browse only: authenticated load needs real sessions."),), size: 8.8pt)
- #rich((("t", "Environment: SWE5001 ECS, CloudFront d3lvq02o2e7tcn.​cloudfront.​net → ALB → ECS Fargate; the README says \"Do not load-test shared SWE5006 dev\". Say \"SWE5001 environment, an image built from dev on 6 Oct\" every time (image 6c7a99ab, 38 backend commits before 9c123c12); never call it a dev result."),), size: 8.8pt)
- #rich((("t", "Target: proposal §6.3 \"Interactive operations respond within 2 seconds under demonstration load (up to 100 concurrent users); team expiry is resolved within 1 minute of window lapse.\" Little's law N = X(R + Z): N = 100, Z = 0.5 s think, R ≈ 0.03 s gives X ≈ 189 requests/s. The 0.5 s think time is our assumption; with longer think times the offered load is lower."),), size: 8.8pt)
- #rich((("t", "History, not the 5.3 result: SWE5001 V2 baseline 16 Oct (docs/swe5001/evidence/20261016-http-baseline-dashboard/README.​md), one monolith task, two runs of 57,600 requests, zero errors, every plateau p95 ≤ 57 ms; saturation not observed, so 200 requests/s is a tested lower bound. Local Node workload 30 Sep (docs/perf/sprint3-baseline.​md): 100 closed-loop VUs, 200 ms think, p95 browse 24 ms, JOIN intent 57 ms, My Orders 18 ms; 30 expiries, worst observation lag 58.18 s. Local only."),), size: 8.8pt)
- #rich((("t", "Expiry on ECS: the V4 burst (2,000 teams, perf/k6/SCALING.​md) has not been run, so expiry evidence is local only. TeamExpirySweepJob runs with fixedDelay PT1M, so the bound is one interval plus the sweep time; measured worst lag 58.18 s with 30 teams (docs/perf/sprint3-baseline.​md). The 5.3 run is the 16 Oct V2 repeat (run 20261016-v2-monolith-repeat, docs/swe5001/evidence/20261016-http-baseline-dashboard/v2-repeat-summary.​json; #670); if a 24 Oct pre-run passes, swap in its numbers."),), size: 8.8pt)
]
